A||||17||DXR_WILL||CARBURETOR
Z||000000||DXR_WILL||08-20-99||06:29 PM||||WOULD I BE BETTER OFF PRODUCING MORE POWER FROM PERFORMANCE BY WHICHING TO A CARBURETOR SET UP FOR MY V6 FIERO? HAS ANYONE DONE THIS BEFORE?  I'M CURIOUS BECAUSE I SAW A PERFORMANCE MANIFOLD AND HOLLY CARB FOR THE CHEVY 60 DEGREE V6 ENGINE.  WITCH I THINK IS THE SAME ENGINE USED IN THE FIERO, RIGHT?  
Z||000001||4Banger Bandit||08-20-99||06:45 PM||||I'm sure most people will say that's a bad idea, but I can see some advantages in it.  You're hp potential will definitely be increased, but reliability and throttle response will suffer in the process.  You will basically be increasing the amount of fuel the engine uses and subsequently gaining a few horses.  My father did something similar to a TPI camaro.  Many people have gotten good results with this, but it's a trade-off.  I like the idea, because I think it would be something new and different, and Holley makes some killer carbs that would work great with it. Correct me if I'm wrong fella's, but you'd be doing-away with the computer and sensors entirely if you did this.  Adjusting carbs is fun too!<p><br>
Z||000002||squid||08-20-99||07:12 PM||||My '85 2.8(coverted to 3.2) has a early '80s s10 vacuum/centrifigal advance distributor and intake thats been ported and adapted to a Holley 350cfm 2 barrel. Its alot easier to access the valve covers and there is very little wiring and no computer but I wouldnt reccomend it if your EFI is working okay. Mine had a porblem no one could fix so after I spent a few $$$ troubleshooting, I decided to fix it my way. 
Z||000003||terryk||08-20-99||07:38 PM||||The Fiero does not need more fuel unless you can burn it. If anything, it needs slightly less. <p>Adding a carb is fine, but the TBI injection is likely to perform better. 
Z||000004||PaUL||08-20-99||07:58 PM||||hey Squid sounds like you got a simillar setup to mine. Im using a distributor from a 1980 citation with edlebrock intake manifold and 390 cfm Holley 4bbl carb.
Z||000005||squid||08-20-99||09:30 PM||||I got my modified stock setup for free(except for the distributor) for putting the Edelbrock setup like Paul has on a s10.
Z||000006||DXR_WILL||08-20-99||09:52 PM||||SQIUD<br>WHAT OTHER MODS DO YOU HAVE BESIDES THE CARB AND MANIFOLD?  YOU CAN MAKE UP FOR THE LOSS OF LOW END IN A HI-PRO CAM AND A NOS KIT?
Z||000007||lowCG||08-20-99||09:59 PM||||After hearing about how good a Fiero worked with fuel injection,and a 290DEG cam,I have to wonder what you'd gain switching back to a carb and HEI,besides losing a few electrical connections,and extra wires.<br>Thought about doing this with my 4 cyl. car.
Z||000008||squid||08-20-99||10:18 PM||||I have 1.6 ratio roller rockers. Mine isnt radical. The only reason I took the injection off is because it wasnt working the way it was supposed to and no matter where I took it, nobody could fix it. Its simple and easy to work on but if I had it to do over I would have just kept trying to fix the injection, especially with the way emissions are now. I kept everthing I took off and I may try to put it all back on eventually. I think a TBI is a great compromise. Only 2 injectors to clog, you can see if they are spraying or leaking, and easy valve cover access.
Z||000009||Cooter||08-20-99||10:44 PM||||I have a Holley Projection 4Di system on my 'Burb and it is almost just like a factory throttle body system. I think that they make a 2bbl version of this injection for 4/6 cylinder engines. THe wiring on the Holley system is fairly simple and you can program it with a laptop and watch the entire computer read out in real time to spot any problems in the fuel system. As an added bonus, the system plugs into the distributer and you can program the timing from the laptop to compensate for gas, altitude etc.. I would much rather have this than another carb.
Z||000010||lowCG||08-21-99||12:52 AM||||The Pro-jection sounds like a cool setup,I always wondered if they were as good as they were advertised to be,do they still sell them?<br>Another system that is easy to adjust,would be the K-jetronic from a Volvo 6 cylinder.Pretty bullet proof also.If only the injector type/size wasn't so different.
Z||000011||Cooter||08-21-99||04:07 PM||||I bought the projection a couple of years ago and as far as I know, they are still available- or at least I hope so in case I need any replacement parts! Going from the carb to the projection made a lot of difference in throttle response and economy. Before I added the aluminum heads and bigger cam, my 6000 pound 3/4 ton 'Burb would get about 15-18 miles to the gallon- not bad without an overdrive and hi-po 454.
Z||000012||lowCG||08-21-99||07:08 PM||||Uh,that's amazing,how about when you're towing something?<br>What kind of roller cam do you have?
Z||000013||Cooter||08-21-99||09:07 PM||||The mileage is not that much different when towing- on one trip from north east AL to central Florida, it got 15 mpg going down there pulling an unloaded single axle car trailer and the trip home with a buick reatta on the trailer it got 18 mpg. The only difference (other than the car on the trailer) was I drove down and my dad drove back- he is much more conservative on speed than I am. The cam is a similiar profile to the new 502 HO crate motor cam. 
Z||000014||theogre||08-21-99||09:25 PM||||changing to a carb, and thus altering emmision controls, may be a legal problem. Be carefull to check local laws.
Z||000015||BOILERMAKER||08-23-99||09:09 PM||||I DIDN'T KNOW CAPS WERE THE "IN" THING NOW.  MAYBE I'LL START USING THEM MORE OFTEN.  I ALWAYS THOUGHT IT MEANT THAT YOU WERE YELLING AT SOMEONE.
Z||000016||DJRice||08-24-99||07:37 AM||||If someone was going to go thru the trouble of switching the intake and injection system, <br>why bother with a carb?  There should be plenty of MPFI or SFI options for the 2.8/3.1.  FI is a precise way to get power and maintain a level of fuel efficiency.<p>At one time, I was considering switching my 84 Buick Lesabre from the CLCC Rochester Quadra-Jet to an EFI because I was tired of trying to make my Carb run right, but Buick finally figured out the problem and I lost interest. <p><br>BTW, In 'chat rooms' the use of all caps was supposed to mean you were yelling.  Personally I like the use of lower case for some reason.<p>
